====================================================================================================
K9  THE COSMOLOGY CHANNEL: on disk, live, and kappa-BLIND
====================================================================================================
  BAO: 7 tracers / 13 numbers (DESI DR2); SNe: 1580 after mask (Pantheon+); CMB: 3 priors
  flat-LCDM fit:      Omega_m=0.3020  h=0.6842  Omega_b h^2=0.02252  chi2=1404.64 / dof=1593
  framework branch:   Omega_m=0.4376  h=0.4704  Omega_b h^2=0.02250  chi2=1403.24   (Om_eff=0.3044)
  Delta chi2 (framework - LCDM) = -1.40  -> the branch is NOT excluded: it is an exact
  reparametrisation, E_fw(z;Om) = E_LCDM(z; Om/(1+Om)).  Verified on the 19 distance numbers:
     shape identity E_fw^2(1+Om) = 1 + Om(1+z)^3 + Or(1+z)^4 : residual 7.1e-15
     -> equivalently E_fw(z;Om) = E_LCDM(z; Om_eff) with Om_eff = Om/(1+Om) = 0.3044
     max |framework/LCDM - 1| over 13 BAO + R + l_A = 2.54e-03
  the branch's OWN h is not robust here: this fit gives h = 0.470, A46 reports 0.568 for the
  same data, and the difference is the radiation bookkeeping inside (1+Om).  So the branch
  determines no H0 that this lane can use: the H0 footing (56.8 / 67.4 / 73.0) is a PRIOR,
  and kappa = a0 sqrt(8pi/3)/(c H0) carries it in full (S_H0 = 0.125 below).
  kappa does NOT enter E(z): d chi2/d kappa = 0 identically.
  K9   PASS  LCDM Om=0.3020 h=0.6842 chi2/dof=0.882 ; framework Om=0.4376 h=0.4704 dchi2=-1.40, distances match to 2.5e-03
        threshold: 0.28 < Om < 0.33, 0.65 < h < 0.71, chi2/dof < 1.05, |dchi2| < 15, distances < 3%, identity < 1e-6   :: the distance vector is live; the framework's background is an EXACT reparametrisation of flat LCDM (so it is not excluded), and its own h is modelling-dependent (0.470 here, 0.568 in A46), so the H0 footing is a prior.  kappa does not enter E(z) at all: the channel supplies H0 and no kappa information

